\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Solver-assisted, exactly certified mesh campaign on the three-branch instance ($\tau =\genfrac  {}{}{}1{1}{5}$, $T=\genfrac  {}{}{}1{6}{5}$): program dimensions ($mQ+1$ variables; $Ms(N_t{+}1)+p_UQ$ inequalities with $s=7$, $p_U=6$, $N_t=T/h$), exact optimal value from \textup  {\hbox {\mathsurround \z@ \normalfont  (\ignorespaces \ref  {eq:meshlaw}\unskip \@@italiccorr )}}, value returned by the HiGHS dual simplex \cite  {HuangfuHall2018} through SciPy, simplex iterations and wall-clock time (single runs on the verification machine, Linux x86\_64, Intel Xeon @ 2.60\,GHz, Python\nobreakspace  {}3.13, SciPy\nobreakspace  {}1.17; counts and times may vary with solver version). Optimality of each exact value is certified by the mesh-independent primal--dual witness pair, independently of the solver. At $h=\genfrac  {}{}{}1{1}{5}$ the witness certifies the value zero; at the finer meshes it is a positive obstruction certificate.\relax }}{11}{table.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:mesh}{{1}{11}{Solver-assisted, exactly certified mesh campaign on the three-branch instance ($\tau =\tfr 15$, $T=\tfr 65$): program dimensions ($mQ+1$ variables; $Ms(N_t{+}1)+p_UQ$ inequalities with $s=7$, $p_U=6$, $N_t=T/h$), exact optimal value from \eqref {eq:meshlaw}, value returned by the HiGHS dual simplex \cite {HuangfuHall2018} through SciPy, simplex iterations and wall-clock time (single runs on the verification machine, Linux x86\_64, Intel Xeon @ 2.60\,GHz, Python~3.13, SciPy~1.17; counts and times may vary with solver version). Optimality of each exact value is certified by the mesh-independent primal--dual witness pair, independently of the solver. At $h=\tfr 15$ the witness certifies the value zero; at the finer meshes it is a positive obstruction certificate.\relax }{table.caption.5}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The mesh law off the uniform family: aligned meshes with unequal blocks, their exact values from \textup  {\hbox {\mathsurround \z@ \normalfont  (\ignorespaces \ref  {eq:meshlaw}\unskip \@@italiccorr )}}, and the solver's returned values (agreement to $10^{-9}$ or better in every case). ``$1+6$'' denotes one blind block and six equal post-observation blocks. The last row is the $2^7$-fold refinement of $\{0,\tau ,T\}$ that first meets the a-priori halting resolution of Remark\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {rem:apriori}.\relax }}{11}{table.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
