\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Mesh study on uniform aligned meshes: the finite value $\rho (h)=\genfrac  {}{}{}1{3}{50}-Th/4$ (exact; solver agreement to $4.2\times 10^{-17}$) converges to the continuous value $\genfrac  {}{}{}1{3}{50}$ from below, while the certified upper bound $\rho (h)+\bar  {e}+Lh_t$ of Theorem\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {thm:bridge}(i) (with $\bar  {e}=Th/4$, $L=\genfrac  {}{}{}1{11}{5}$, $h_t=h/2$) converges from above. The dotted line marks the a-priori halting resolution $h<\genfrac  {}{}{}1{3}{340}$ of Theorem\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {thm:bridge}(iii); every uniform aligned mesh with $h<\genfrac  {}{}{}1{1}{5}$ already certifies.\relax }}{12}{figure.caption.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:mesh}{{2}{12}{Mesh study on uniform aligned meshes: the finite value $\rho (h)=\tfr 3{50}-Th/4$ (exact; solver agreement to $4.2\times 10^{-17}$) converges to the continuous value $\tfr 3{50}$ from below, while the certified upper bound $\rho (h)+\ebar +Lh_t$ of Theorem~\ref {thm:bridge}(i) (with $\ebar =Th/4$, $L=\tfr {11}5$, $h_t=h/2$) converges from above. The dotted line marks the a-priori halting resolution $h<\tfr 3{340}$ of Theorem~\ref {thm:bridge}(iii); every uniform aligned mesh with $h<\tfr 15$ already certifies.\relax }{figure.caption.7}{}}
