\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces The shared-authority ladder. Certificate margins as functions of the observation delay: the triple's $\Gamma (\tau )=\tau -\genfrac  {}{}{}1{7}{50}$ and the two-label pair duals $\Gamma _B(\tau )$ of \textup  {\hbox {\mathsurround \z@ \normalfont  (\ignorespaces \ref  {eq:pairdual}\unskip \@@italiccorr )}}, plotted where their label time stays inside the horizon. Zero crossings are the exact thresholds $\genfrac  {}{}{}1{7}{50}<\genfrac  {}{}{}1{15-\sqrt  {183}}{6}<\genfrac  {}{}{}1{10-\sqrt  {58}}{6}$; the audited delay $\tau =\genfrac  {}{}{}1{1}{5}$ lies strictly inside both pair rungs and outside the triple's.\relax }}{14}{figure.caption.9}\protected@file@percent }
